  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 233 AM EDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nForecast on track. This morning lows shaping up as advertised. A\nfew locations north of US-6 is trending to reach down into the\nupper 30s. Dew points have stayed elevated (mainly in the lower\n40s) which will keep temperatures from dropping much further.\nCurrent temps here at the forecast office is 45 degrees as of\n2:30 AM EDT. \n\nTemperatures will rebound nicely later today with western\nportions of the CWA getting into the lower 70s with slight upper\nlevel ridging pushing across the Great Lakes region. Breezy\nsoutherly winds with a few gusts to around 20 mph later today \ninto Wednesday. Wednesday looks to be warmer yet with most \nlocations reaching into the 70s and even a few locations mainly \nsouth and west parts of the area getting near the 80 degree \nmark. Another weak upper level trough will then push into the \nregion by Thursday and this will bring a an increase in clouds \nand a shot of cooler temperatures for Thursday and Friday with \nhighs in the upper 60s to low 70s each day. Temperatures warm \nonce again this weekend into the beginning of next week with \nhighs back into the 70s across the area with a few locations \nagain getting close to 80. Precipitation chances remain nil \nthrough the forecast until late into this weekend for Sunday and\nat this time looks to be only for the far southeastern portions\nof the CWA with that tropical disturbance pushing northeastward\nfrom TX and into the Ohio Valley.",
